\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Architecture \'97 a six-stage cascade\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 The whole design turns on one number: a vision model over a few thousand images is too slow for a single day, so almost nothing should reach it. Stages 2 and 3 exist purely to protect stage 4. Build it in this order, and measure throughput in the first 30 minutes before writing anything else \'97 one image timed end-to-end through stage 4, fifty images timed through stages 2\'963. Those two numbers decide whether the 800-image cap is realistic or needs to drop to 300.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Ingest
\f1\b0  
\f2\i (seconds/image)
\f1\i0  \'97 point at a local folder; decode HEIC to JPEG up front with 
\f3\fs26 pillow-heif
\f1\fs24 . In parallel, Nango pulls Gmail attachments (images and PDFs) into the same staging directory. Every file lands with a 
\f3\fs26 source
\f1\fs24  tag (
\f3\fs26 photos
\f1\fs24  | 
\f3\fs26 gmail
\f1\fs24 ).\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Metadata gate \'97 free
\f1\b0  
\f2\i (~0 ms/image)
\f1\i0  \'97 no model. Use filename heuristics, EXIF, aspect ratio, and dimensions to cheaply demote obvious non-documents (blurry, very wide, tiny). Keep this loose; its job is to filter, not decide.\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 OCR gate \'97 cheap
\f1\b0  
\f2\i (~100\'96300 ms/image)
\f1\i0  \'97 run 
\f3\fs26 tesseract
\f1\fs24  over survivors, count confident words, drop anything under a threshold (start at 8 words). Keep the OCR text \'97 it's reused as a hint in stage 4 and as search fallback.\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Extract \'97 expensive, should hit ~5% of the library
\f1\b0  
\f2\i (~1\'963 s/image)
\f1\i0  \'97 Gemma 4 vision on the image plus OCR text as a hint, one call, returning one strict JSON object (schema below). Classify the doc type and pull fields in the same pass.\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Cross-check \'97 the confidence signal
\f1\b0  
\f2\i (on a sampled subset)
\f1\i0  \'97 route the same image to a second, larger Gemma checkpoint through Respan and diff the JSON field by field. Agreement = high confidence; disagreement flags the record for human review in the UI. 
\f0\b This second model must be hosted on Lambda, and it must be a Gemma checkpoint
\f1\b0  \'97 that single deployment decision satisfies both the Lambda rubric line and the Gemma-on-Lambda bonus, so don't host anything else there.\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	6	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Store & search
\f1\b0  
\f2\i (instant)
\f1\i0  \'97 SQLite with an FTS5 virtual table over extracted fields and OCR text. No vector DB.\
